'''Tolomar Reez''' was a [[human]] from the [[planet]] [[Nar Kanji]] who served in the criminal gang known as [[Kanjiklub]] under [[topboss]] [[Tasu Leech]]. In [[34 ABY]], he accompanied Leech and several other Kanjiklub members, as well as members of the [[Guavian Death Gang]], in [[Skirmish aboard the Eravana|boarding]] the ''[[Eravana]]'', a [[Baleen-class heavy freighter|freighter]] belonging to the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]], who owed both gangs [[Galactic Credit Standard|money]].

Solo argued with Leech and the Death Gang's frontman, [[Bala-Tik]], in one of the [[freighter]]'s corridors until a trio of [[Death|deadly]] [[rathtar]]s that the smuggler had captured attacked both gangs. Reez became separated from his comrades while fleeing from the rathtars and then ran into Solo, who punched him in the face and hurled him into the [[mouth]] of a rathtar.

==Biography==
===Debt collecting===
[[File:Kanjiklub.png|thumb|left|225px|Tolomar Reez (far left) was a member of the Kanjiklub criminal outfit.]]
Tolomar Reez<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/749616406245699584|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2016-07-03|quote=@LelalMekha Yeah, same with Infinity.|archivefile=File:PabloHidalgo-LegoName-Twitter.png|nolive=1}} {{C|In response to: "@pablohidalgo <nowiki>youtube.com/watch?v=JwxAeHPLpPg</nowiki> The Lego game identifies a few BG characters from TFA, but are those names canonical?"}} &mdash; [[Pablo Hidalgo]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] confirmed that character names introduced in ''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]'' are considered [[canon]], despite the [[Star Wars video games|video game]] itself being non-canon.</ref> was a [[Homeworld|native]] of the [[planet]] [[Nar Kanji]]<ref name="Homeworld" /> who served in the criminal group known as [[Kanjiklub]] during the [[Cold War]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]].<ref name="TFA" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> he<ref name="TFAn" /> and four other members of the gang accompanied their<ref name="TFA" /> [[topboss]],<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref> [[Tasu Leech]], in tracking down the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] so that they could reclaim a loan of 50,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] Solo had borrowed from Kanjiklub in order to hunt [[rathtar]]s. Leech made an alliance with the [[Guavian Death Gang]]&mdash;another criminal group to whom Solo owed money&mdash;before [[Skirmish aboard the Eravana|confronting]] the smuggler, and both groups boarded Solo's [[Baleen-class heavy freighter|''Baleen''-class heavy freighter]] ''[[Eravana]]'' above the planet [[Jakku]].<ref name="TFA" />

Reez and the other Kanjiklub members marched through the ''Eravana''{{'s}} corridors until they found Solo and his [[Wookiee]] partner, [[Chewbacca]], already arguing about their debts with the Death Gang's frontman, [[Bala-Tik]]. Reez then stood menacingly beside Leech as the head of Kanjiklub joined the argument, which continued until Bala-Tik recognized Solo's other companion, the [[BB-series astromech droid|astromech droid]] [[BB-8]], as a fugitive wanted by the First Order.<ref name="TFA" />

===Rathtar chow===
{{Quote|Search the freighter.|Razoo Qin-Fee gives orders to Kanjiklub|translated=1|audio=Qin-Fee-Search.flac|<ref name="TFA" />}}
[[File:Reez_gets_munched.png|thumb|right|225px|A rathtar consumed Tolomar Reez aboard the ''Eravana''.]]
[[Razoo Qin-Fee]], Leech's [[Lieutenant (criminal)|lieutenant]],<ref name="TFAVD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> ordered Kanjklub to begin searching the [[freighter]] for another pair of fugitives associated with BB-8; however, Reez and everyone else in the corridor were quickly distracted from the [[Astromech droid|droid]] by the howls of three rathtars that Solo had managed to capture. The rathtars had been released accidentally by the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], one of the two fugitives that Kanjiklub was looking for.<ref name="TFA" />

One of the rathtars then barreled into the corridor behind the Kanjiklub members, grabbing two of them and forcing the remainder to flee down another corridor to their right. Reez became separated from his comrades as he fled and ended up crossing paths with Solo. The smuggler punched Reez in the face as he turned a corner, grabbing the Kanjiklub member by his torso and hurling him directly into the [[mouth]] of a rathtar that had been chasing Solo, Chewbacca, and BB-8. The rathtar consumed Reez whole, belching out only one of his [[boot]]s.<ref name="TFA" />

==Personality and traits==
Reez was a [[human]] male with [[Color|tan]] skin and black [[hair]].<ref name="TFA" />

==Equipment==
Reez wore a brown suit of [[armor]] over a yellow [[Clothing|tunic]] with a [[helmet]] that included [[goggles]] to cover his [[eye]]s. He carried a [[boiler rifle]] while onboard the ''Eravana''.<ref name="TFA" />

==Behind the scenes==
Tolomar Reez first appeared in the [[2015]] [[sequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. The actor playing him was not credited, and the character did not receive a name in the film<ref name="TFA" /> but was identified by the [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]'', which was released in conjunction with ''The Force Awakens''.<ref name="DI3.0">''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]''</ref> Despite the game being [[Canon|non-canon]], [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] confirmed that the names provided by the game for previously unidentified characters, including Reez, were considered canon.<ref name="Twitter" /> In the game, all basic Kanjiklub enemies share his appearance.<ref name="DI3.0" />

In the [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novelization)|novelization]] of ''The Force Awakens'', written by [[Alan Dean Foster]], Han Solo is described as hurling a member of the Guavian Death Gang into the mouth of a rathtar instead of Reez.<ref name="TFAn" /> In [[2016]] non-canon video game ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'', Reez can be unlocked as a playable character under the name "Kanjiklub (Sniper)" by completing the mission "Chapter 4: The ''Eravana''."<ref name="LEGOTFA">''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]''</ref> In the [[2022]] non-canon video game ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]'', Reez appears in the mission "Reap What You Solo," an adaptation of the events on the '' Eravana'' from ''The Force Awakens''.<ref name="LSS">''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]''</ref>

[[File:Kanjiklub-LSS.png|thumb|right|300px|Tolomar Reez (right) wields two knives in ''LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga''.]]
He is depicted wielding two [[Knife|knives]] instead of a rifle when Kanjiklub first confront Solo but later uses a rifle when attacking the smuggler and his allies in the [[hangar]] where Solo's [[YT-1300 light freighter]], the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', is parked. After the players defeat Reez, he is then shown arriving in the hangar again alongside<ref name="LSS" /> fellow Kanjiklub member [[Crokind Shand]]<ref name="TFAVD" /> as well as Bala-Tik and several [[Guavian security soldier]]s. The group is all then blown to the floor by the [[engine]]s of the ''Falcon'' as it takes off from the hangar.<ref name="LSS" />

